{"type":"message","id":"8e86b9c8","parentId":"c1d45473","timestamp":"2026-02-18T22:00:08.541Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Initiating Weather Retrieval**\n\nI'm currently focused on retrieving the weather for Seoul, as requested. My initial approach involves checking for a `weather` command-line interface or related tools via `exec`. If that proves unsuccessful, I'll need to use an alternative method.\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<think>The user wants a morning briefing for Sam.\nI need to:\n1.  **Check the weather in Seoul.** I don't have a direct `weather` tool, but the prompt mentions \"using weather skill\". I should check if there's a `weather` CLI or similar available via `exec`. If not, I can use `web_fetch` to get the weather from a site like wttr.in. The `TOOLS.md` or `AGENTS.md` might have hints, but I don't see a specific weather tool in the provided context. I'll use `web_fetch` on `https://wttr.in/Seoul?format=3` or similar for a quick check, or a full page if needed. Actually, `web_fetch` on `https://wttr.in/Seoul` is a good standard way for agents to get weather.\n2.  **System status overview.** I can use `session_status` to get the current session info. I can also check `openclaw gateway status` via `exec` to see if the gateway is healthy.\n3.  **Urgent notifications/tasks from memory.** I need to read `memory/2026-02-18.md` (yesterday) and `memory/2026-02-19.md` (today, likely empty or just created) to see if there are carry-over tasks. I should also check `MEMORY.md` for high-level context if relevant, but daily notes are better for \"urgent\" things.\n\nPlan:\n1.  Fetch weather for Seoul.\n2.  Check gateway status.\n3.  Read recent memory files.\n4.  Compile the briefing.</think>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"web_fetch_1771452007926_27","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://wttr.in/Seoul?0T"},"thoughtSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_1771452008097_28","name":"exec","arguments":{"comm